+## 19:51 - Transient LLM retry with exponential backoff (PLAN-012)
+
+**Scope:** server/translate | **Type:** Feature | **Commit:** 14c7f52 @ doc-centric
+
+## Scope
+server/translate
+
+## Type
+Feature
+
+## Commit
+- **Hash:** 14c7f52
+- **Repo:** doc-centric
+- **Message:** Retry transient LLM failures with exponential backoff (PLAN-012)
+- **Author:** Satoshi Man <mrvuong.bitcoin@gmail.com>
+- **Date:** 2026-11-05 19:51:00 +0700
+
+## User request
+Add retry with exponential backoff for translation API calls: transient failures only (network, 5xx, 429), 500ms base doubling up to 3 attempts with jitter, immediate failure on other 4xx and malformed responses, same error path on exhaustion, tests must not hit the real API. Done when npm test and npm run typecheck pass.
+
+## Reason
+Transient provider blips previously burned the single primary->fallback hop and the session-level queued retry. In-request exponential backoff (PLAN-012, verified against ADR-003/BDR-002, review_count 1) absorbs them cheaply; exhaustion still surfaces as TranslationError through translateSegment unchanged.
+
+## Description
+Added withRetry + isTransientLlmError in server/translate/retry.ts and wrapped chat.completions.create in OpenAICompatTranslator.request. Retryable: HTTP 429/5xx and status-less transport failures; other 4xx and post-response TranslationErrors fail immediately. Backoff: 500ms base doubling, +/-10% jitter, 3 attempts per endpoint (primary then fallback chain unchanged per ADR-003). New retry.test.ts plus translator-level tests for 5xx/429/network retry, 4xx immediate failure, 3-attempt exhaustion, and malformed-response no-retry.
+
+## Files changed
+server/translate/retry.ts
+server/translate/retry.test.ts
+server/translate/openai-compat.ts
+server/translate/openai-compat.test.ts
+CONTEXTS/03-implement-plan/PLAN-012-llm-transient-retry.md
+
+## Notes
+Retry-After header not honored; assist path intentionally untouched (PLAN-009 pinned best-effort single attempt); worst case 3x3 plus fallback provider calls per segment under sustained outage.
+
